WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.380
What if you were asked to find the HCF and

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.720
LCM of 16 and 20?

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.960
You have two options.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.720
Either you find the HCF and LCM separately.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.400
Or we find them together.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.000
Of course we will find them together.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.200
All we need to do

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.360
is use the common division method of finding the LCM.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.540
In the first step,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.040
we write the numbers separated by a comma.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.100
And then draw an L shaped line like this.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.560
Then we look for a common factor of the two numbers,

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.580
and write it here.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.140
2 is common factor of both the numbers.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.000
Then we write the quotients underneath.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.880
2 times 8 is 16.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.100
And 2 times 10 is 20.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.640
Since these numbers are not co-prime

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.100
we go back to the second step and continue the process.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.580
They have two as the common factor.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.540
And 2 times 4 is 8.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.400
2 times 5 is 10.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:28.420
We stop here since 4 &amp; 5 are co-prime numbers.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.340
They have no common factors except 1.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.320
The product of the numbers in this L shape

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.980
gives us the LCM of the two numbers.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:44.560
The LCM equals 2 times 2, times 4, times 5.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:50.020
That is 4 multiplied by 20 which equals 80.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:50.940
Yes,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.500
but how does this give us the HCF?

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:54.420
Well,

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.560
the product of the factors on the left gives us the HCF.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:04.200
Hence, the HCF will equal 2 times 2 which is 4.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.500
This is the HCF of 16 and 20.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.020
So you can see that just this one method

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:16.400
gave us the HCF as well as the LCM of two numbers.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:22.360
But we also have to note that this works only for two numbers.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.020
There is another interesting concept above the HCF

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.860
and the LCM of two numbers.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:33.640
First, let's find the product of the LCM and the HCF.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.280
LCM is 80 and the HCF is 4.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:44.280
The product will be 80 times 4 which equals 320.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.500
Now let's find the product of the two numbers.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.520
It will be 16 times 20

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.620
which equals 320.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.760
This will always be true!

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.060
For any two given numbers,

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.180
the product of their LCM and HCF

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:05.400
will be equal to the product of the two given numbers.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.260
 

